      "body": "**Missing: connection/credential recovery before exhaustion.** Per the issue's restart-cures evidence (identical history succeeds after a plain process restart), repeated deterministic `finish_reason: error` failures are most likely a stale pooled keep-alive connection or a stale copilot token — yet every attempt in this ladder still rides the SAME cached shared client (`provider_common.dart:1146-1180` already exposes the drop-cache seam). On the 2nd consecutive identical failure, drop the cached shared client and re-dial (and attempt a token refresh on the copilot path) before declaring exhaustion. Add the issue's fake-transport test: pooled connection always errors, a fresh connection succeeds — the retry logic must recover by re-dialing instead of failing 3× on the dead connection. The probable-overflow terminal stays correct for the genuine large-request case; it just must not mask the recoverable connection case."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "rootCommentId": 4727406517,
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDOTXdlLc69EtiH",
      "path": "lib/src/cli/agent_cli_compaction.dart",
      "line": 1801,
      "resolved": false,
      "bot": false,
      "body": "⚠️ severity: IMPORTANT —\n⚠️ **IMPORTANT: the forensics/settlement log was not extended to the new stop class — the gh-241 #5e invariant breaks for probable-overflow stops**\n\nThis PR extends `_contextStopContinuationArmed` so a probable-overflow stop arms the persist → auto-compact → continue funnel. That predicate's doc contract (and gh-241 follow-up #5e, E2) is that it is **shared with the forensics log \"so the forensics log and the settlement can never disagree\"** — but only the funnel side was extended; the stash side was not.\n\n`lib/src/cli/approval_commands.dart:1210-1216` stashes `_pendingContextStop` only on\n`isContextWindowExhaustedError(...)` — the probable-overflow story carries the `probable context overflow` marker, not `Context window exhausted`, so for this class:\n\n1. `TurnEndEvent` falls to the else branch and logs `turn end … stop=error` immediately;\n2. `AgentEndEvent` sees `_pendingContextStop == null` and logs `run end` — while `_maybeOverWindowContinue` is about to compact and continue;\n3. `_settleContextStopLog(ContextStopOutcome.compacting)` (agent_cli_compaction.dart:1809) then no-ops because the stash is empty — the settlement and the forensics log disagree, exactly the shape gh-241 #5e exists to prevent.\n\nThe trail for every probable-overflow stop therefore reads `turn end … stop=error` + `run end` + a second full run's logs, where the pinned guard-class contract is **`stop=compacting (continuation pending)`, no `stop=error`, `run end` exactly once** (test/cli/agent_cli_over_window_continuation_retry_test.dart:281-293). Post-mortem analysis of the very incident class this ticket targets (the 14:52 / 15:37 failures) will misread the run boundary.\n\n**Fix**: stash on the same armed predicate the funnel uses — e.g. at `approval_commands.dart:1212` match `isContextWindowExhaustedError(...) || isProbableOverflowError(...)` (the `_contextStopIsProbableOverflow` flag then keeps picking the notice class). Add an e2e log assertion for the probable-overflow stop mirroring the guard-class one, so the shared-predicate contract stays pinned for both classes."
    }
  ],
